coder › Done on branch `work/env-config` (4 commits on top of `44f0e54`).

What changed:
- `src/env.ts` (new): exports `fromEnv(env, prefix = 'APP_'): Partial<Config>`. Reads `APP_PORT` (via `Number()`, `TypeError` naming `APP_PORT` on `NaN`), `APP_HOST`/`APP_NAME` as strings, `APP_DEBUG` case-insensitively (`true`/`1`/`yes` → true, `false`/`0`/`no` → false, else `TypeError` naming `APP_DEBUG`). Absent (`undefined`) or empty (`''`) values are left out.
- `src/config.ts`: added `validate(config): Config` returning the config, else `TypeError` naming the field: port must be an integer 1–65535, host/name must not be empty.
- `src/index.ts`: `resolveConfig(file = {}, env = process.env)` — file over `DEFAULTS`, `fromEnv(env)` over both, then `validate`.
- Tests: new `src/env.test.ts` (parsing, prefix, absent/empty, both `TypeError`s), new `src/config.test.ts` (valid passthrough, bad ports incl. `NaN`/float, empty host/name), extended `src/index.test.ts` (env-over-file precedence, validation of the merged result, env parse errors propagate).

