Decisions the task did not spell out:
- `fromEnv` accepts any `Number()`-parseable port (e.g. floats) and leaves integer/range enforcement to `validate`, so `APP_PORT=3000.5` parses then fails validation with `port`.
- Empty means exactly `''` (plus `undefined`); whitespace-only strings are not treated as empty and flow through normal parsing/validation.
- `validate` returns the same object (`toBe` identity holds), and error messages embed the field/variable name (`APP_PORT`, `APP_DEBUG`, `port`, `host`, `name`).

